result.summary:
The baseline engine reads no market metadata at all: no syminfo.type, session, root or current_contract, and no measured session shape. Every symbol gets the same New-York-time sessions, killzones and wall-clock bar counts. That produces visible mislabels:
- "LDN H/L" on a US-stock extended chart is the 04:00-05:00 pre-market;
- killzones and session pools fire on crypto weekends;
- stock PD/PW freshness runs 1.9-2.3x too slow;
- stub days (the 2025-11-27/28 CME outage, Sunday candles on 00:00-UTC FX feeds) are pushed as full PDH/PDL.

Gap-throughs are a large share of sweeps on gappy assets, and the engine feeds all of them into the draw vector D as raids:
- GOOG daily: 38% of PDH takes and 29% of PDL takes open beyond the level;
- ES/NQ 1H: about 10% of PD takes are gap-throughs at the session open, 38% on Sunday opens.

B's re-tests overturned three of A's headline effects:
- a Tokyo-local Asia range is not a better London/NY target than the ICT NY-fixed range (logit +0.03, 95% CI -0.05 to 0.11, 590 day-symbols), so the DST clock is a convention and A's ASSET-2 is dropped (London DST is already in TIME-1e);
- the BTC weekend range is taken at the weekday rate at equal distance (52% vs 52% at 0.25-0.5 ADR); A's +9-12 pp came from counting either side and a weekend-deflated ADR;
- the 17:00 NY rollover hour on EURUSD 1H shows no excess fake sweeps (break rate 10% vs 19%, wick-only share 0.43 vs 0.52).

Continuous-futures rolls are a real artefact on TradingView's default unadjusted charts (about +40-50 ES points per quarter at 2025-26 carry). One back-adjusted request detects every historical roll exactly, but a roll during a live session only shows after the chart reloads.

Scheduled events concentrate liquidity runs in time and differ by asset: FOMC 14:00 bar 4.9x normal on gold, 2.7x on ES, 1.3x on crude; jumps follow FOMC, NFP and claims (Lee 2012); book depth falls in the release minute. A release-bar sweep is news repricing, not a raid.

Event calendars are fragile:
- the 2025-26 shutdowns moved NFP to a Thursday, a Tuesday and a Wednesday;
- the Fed revised its 2027 FOMC calendar on 2026-11-12 (December moved to November 17; October became strategy-only).

Recurring rules are therefore only "possible" events and date lists must be user-maintained.

Several of A's facts and Pine claims needed correction:
- CME 24/7 crypto went live on 2026-05-29, not 06-01;
- syminfo.volumetype "n/a" does not mean "no volume" (documented);
- the gap test must use the level's near edge;
- the registry loop does not feed liqEvt;
- holiday-day extremes are not weaker next-day targets.

The best fixes are a market profile with a session-coverage guard, a gap-through guard, and a measured bar clock with stub-day merging (all P1). Next come a one-request roll handler, an asset-aware event calendar on top of TIME-8, and RTH H/L from a chart-side tracker (all P2).

concepts.definition:
Exchange opens follow local clocks:
- Tokyo 09:00 JST = 20:00 EDT / 19:00 EST;
- Shanghai/HK 09:00-09:30 = 20:00-20:30 EST;
- Frankfurt 08:00 CET and London 08:00 = 02:00/03:00 ET, except 03:00/04:00 in the US/EU mismatch weeks (2026: Mar 8-29 and Oct 25-Nov 1).

ICT keeps fixed New York times.

concepts.evidenceNotes:
Activity data:
- the index-futures 03:00->04:00 spike moves on 93% of mismatch days (n=15) [A];
- EUR/GBP futures keep a 02:00 bump in the mismatch weeks too (+0.50), so the Frankfurt shift is not clean [B-corrected];
- in US winter both 19:00 and 20:00 ET show bumps.

Forecasting value: none. A Tokyo-local Asia range (19:00-23:00 EST) is taken by London+NY at the same rate as the ICT 20:00-00:00 range at equal distance (logit +0.031, 95% CI -0.053 to 0.112, 1,440 sides / 590 day-symbols, 7 CME symbols) [B asia_clock.py]. Ito & Hashimoto 2006: activity follows local hours.

B gap_share.py:
- GOOG daily 2004-13: 38.4% of PDH takes and 29.4% of PDL takes are gap-throughs;
- ES/NQ 1H: 10.3%/10.0% of PD-level takes, 37.9%/37.5% on Sunday opens;
- CL 8.6% (Sunday 23.1%);
- SI 3.4% (16.4%).

concepts.definition:
TradingView aligns intraday bars to the session start:
- CME 4H at 18/22/02/06/10/14 ET;
- FX at 17:00;
- crypto at 00:00 UTC;
- US stocks RTH 1H at 09:30, and 4H = 09:30-13:30 plus a 2.5-hour bar.

concepts.evidenceNotes:
B gap_atr.py:
