concepts.evidenceNotes:
This study's data:
- Thursday 08:00-hour bar: ES 1.33 vs Mon 1.02, GC 1.75 vs 1.27;
- FOMC 14:00 bar: ES 2.70x, NQ 2.32x, GC 4.88x, CL 1.34x (n=8) [A].

Literature:
- Ederington & Lee 1993/1995: adjustment begins within about 10 s and is mostly done by about 40 s; small overreaction corrected in minutes 2-3; volatility elevated about 15 min;
- Lee 2012 RFS: jumps follow FOMC, NFP and claims;
- Scholtus et al. 2014 JBF: book depth falls in the release minute;
- ABDV 2003.

B-corrected: A's 'later moves unrelated to the first minute' is unverified. Calendar fragility: shutdowns moved NFP to 2025-11-20 (Thu), 2025-12-16 (Tue) and 2026-02-11 (Wed); the Fed revised its 2027 calendar on 2026-11-12.

concepts.definition:
Documented return patterns by time of day:
- S&P futures overnight drift at 02:00-03:00 ET, about 3.7% p.a. 1998-2019, about 0 since 2021;
- dollar up before the Tokyo/Frankfurt/London fixes and down after (a W shape);
- the first half-hour predicts the last half-hour (R2 about 1.6%);
- gold positive at night, negative by day.

Trading-hour changes that move day definitions and session sets:
- CME crypto futures 24/7 since 2026-05-29;
- NYSE 22-hour initial approval (Feb 2025);
- SEC approved Nasdaq extended hours 2026-04-10, with a planned start on Sun 2026-12-06 (unconfirmed);
