proposals.rationale:
With TradingView's default unadjusted continuous futures, each roll (4 a year on index, 12 on CL, 6 on GC) jumps by the carry (ES +40-50 points, about 6x a median 1-h range). The jump:
- sweeps pools;
- creates fake FVGs and displacement;
- corrupts the ATR and excursion surface (CAL-10);
- shifts every distance.

proposals.spec:
Same-timeframe detection with one request:
- isCont = syminfo.type == "futures" and not na(syminfo.current_contract);
- tkAdj = isCont ? ticker.modify(syminfo.tickerid, backadjustment = backadjustment.on) : syminfo.tickerid;
- cAdj = request.security(tkAdj, timeframe.period, close);
- adjD = isCont ? close - nz(cAdj, close) : 0;
- rollJ = adjD - nz(adjD[1], adjD);
- rollBar = |rollJ| > 2 x mintick and barstate.isconfirmed.
If the user enabled B-ADJ, adjD is 0 and the handler is a no-op.

Phase 1 (S), on rollBar:
- skip FVG/OB creation and dispUp/dispDn for this bar and the next 2;
- apply ASSET-2 gap rules to sweeps;
- export rollBar to CAL-10 so surface windows containing it are skipped;
- panel shows '⚠ ROLL +x — enable B-ADJ' for 50 bars.

Phase 2 (M): input rollMode = Shift levels | Drop levels | Ignore. 'Shift' adds rollJ to:
- pool price/top/bottom/oTop/oBot;
- extReg px;
- iFVG trackers;
- aPDH/aPDL/aPWH/aPWL;
- the open anchors;
- obSwingH/L;
- open Trials (edge/inv/entry).
Tooltips say 'roll-adjusted +x'.

proposals.rationale:
